        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3EOnVQmZOxO2PskyNB4L-30" parent="3EOnVQmZOxO2PskyNB4L-1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;It will always start with the five-second countdown&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If the pause button is pressed, it will become a resume button, and at the top there will be a &quot;End&quot; button.&amp;nbsp;And the timer type drop-down will reappear&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This screen shows five mock-ups. The first is showing the mock-up right after you start the circuit. Every circuit will automatically start with a countdown from five seconds. The second mock-up shows just after the first exercise has started. It&#39;ll have the timer, the name of the exercise, and then the next exercise.&amp;nbsp;The third mock-up shows the transition timer between exercises that&#39;s labeled as rest time in the table. The fourth mock-up is basically the same as the second mock-up, and the fifth mock-up shows what happens if you pause a workout&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="417" width="321" x="-72" y="376" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
